hark ask intermittently fails before listen with Gemini TTS HTTP 400: model tried to generate text but should only be used for TTS. Ordinary planning questions trigger it under provider=auto/google; retrying a shorter prompt often works. Need provider fallback/retry so ask remains usable.

GitHub: https://github.com/ultradyn/hark/issues/9 (this bl item and that issue are the same bug — B177 was filed locally, #9 upstream).

Current state verified 2026-08-23: still unfixed. No TTS provider fallback exists in src/hark/speech.py (no fallback / next_provider / try_next logic on the TTS path).

Repro from #9: [tts] provider="auto", disabled=["xai","openai"], then
  hark tts --no-play --standalone "Quick question about the diagram. Should the main message be that every chain is protected by the whole network?"
-> HTTP 400 "Model tried to generate text, but it should only be used for TTS". Reproduced consistently 2026-08-17. Plain statements ("Testing one two three.") synthesize fine; nearly any substantive QUESTION fails. Content-dependent and nondeterministic — the very first question of a session succeeded, then 6+ consecutive failures.

Impact: with xai/openai disabled in config, auto lands on google and `hark ask` becomes unusable for its core purpose — asking questions. That session had to hand-switch to minimax, which then hit B187/gh-10.

DESIGN DECISION (coordinator, 2026-08-23): fix BOTH halves, and treat the fallback as the load-bearing one.
1. Provider fallback (required): on a TTS error of this class, retry once, then fall back to the next enabled provider, rather than failing the whole ask with exit 4 while the operator is already waiting. The fallback must be observable — say which provider actually spoke, in the JSON and in the logs, so a silent downgrade never looks like a success.
2. Model/request hardening (best-effort): pin a TTS-only Gemini model or shape the request so the model cannot "answer" instead of speaking. Do this if it is cheap, but do not let it substitute for (1) — a content-dependent, nondeterministic upstream 400 will find a new trigger.

Sequencing: land AFTER B187/gh-10 (split --tts-provider / --stt-provider). Both touch provider resolution, and having a clean per-leg provider first means the fallback only has to walk the TTS chain.

Do not add a blanket retry-on-any-error: scope the retry to this error class so a real auth or quota failure still fails fast (cf. B175, doctor reporting ready on a bad token).

Reopened 2026-10-26 during full B135-up audit: real decoded subprocess ProviderError terminalizes shared synthesis pool via cancel, preventing B177 retry/fallback although in-process tests passed. Decision: structured provider errors normally reap/release authority while actual timeout/interruption still cancels. Covered in provider lane B164/B181; add real subprocess retry/handover regressions before closure.

Implementation/decision receipt 2026-10-26: Real subprocess provider verdict now reaps/releases normally so same owner can retry/fallback; genuine deadline/interrupt still cancels. Preserved B177 content-error scope and separate B164 auto-auth behavior. Independent review and parent review completed; isolated-worktree code merged to master. Final combined remote gate pending.

Final verification 2026-10-26: reviewed fix merged to master. Integrated x-tall CPython3.13.11 suite: 6525 passed, 104 skipped, 0 failed in151.61s. Independent review and parent review passed. Full receipt /tmp/hark-b135-full-final.log; per-task evidence and design above.